      \field{sortinithash}{d7095fff47cda75ca2589920aae98399}
      \field{labelnamesource}{author}
      \field{labeltitlesource}{title}
      \field{abstract}{We generalize the Lefschetz trace formula to certain algebraic stacks. Let X be a smooth Deligne-Mumford stack of finite type over the finite field ${\rm I\!F}\sb{q}.$ Let $\Phi\sb{q}$ be the arithmetic Frobenius acting on the $\ell$-adic cohomology of X. Then we have$${\rm tr}\Phi\sb{q}\mid H\sp*(\bar{\bf X}\sb{sm}, \doubq\sb\ell) = {\sum\limits\sb{\xi\in\lbrack{\mathcal{X}}({\rm I\!F}\sb{q})\rbrack}}\ {1 \over \#\rm Aut\ \xi}.$$Now let X be as above and let G be a linear algebraic group over ${\rm I\!F}\sb{q},$ acting on X. Let ${\bf Y} = \lbrack{\bf X}/G\rbrack$ be the corresponding Artin stack. Then we have (for any embedding $\doubq\sb\ell\to \doubc)$ the Lefschetz trace formula$${\rm tr}\Phi\sb{q}\mid H\sp*(\bar{\bf Y}\sb{\rm sm}, \doubc)={\sum\limits\sb{\xi\in\lbrack{\bf Y}({\rm I\!F}\sb{q})\rbrack}}\ {1\over \#\rm Aut\ \xi}.\eqno(0.1)$$Here the left hand side is usually an infinite series. On the other hand, we study reductive group schemes over curves and their principal homogeneous bundles. So let G be a reductive group scheme over the curve X over the field k. We prove that there exists a canonical parabolic subgroup P of G, characterized by the facts that the numerical invariants of P are positive and $P/R\sb{u}(P)$ is semi-stable. The degree of P is the degree of instability of G. We conjecture that $H\sp0(X,{\bf g}/{\bf p}) = 0,$ where g and p are the lie algebras of G and P, respectively. To study reductive group schemes, we introduce root systems with complementary convex solids and prove that they have unique special facets. We apply our results to the algebraic stack H$\sp1(X, G)$ of principal homogeneous G-bundles (or torsors). Let H$\sbsp{d}{1}(X, G)$ be the substack of G-torsors of degree d. We introduce a natural stratification $({\bf H}\sbsp{d}{1}(X,G)\sb{\bf v})\sb{{\bf v}\in{\bf V}}$ of ${\bf H}\sbsp{d}{1}(X, G),$ parametrized by the non-negative elements in the free abelian group V on the connected components of the scheme of Dynkin diagrams of G. Let ${\bf H}\sbsp{d}{1}(X, G)\sb{\leq m}$ be the stack of G-torsors of degree d and degree of instability less than or equal to m. Then ${\bf H}\sbsp{d}{1}(X, G)\sb{\leq m}$ is smooth of finite type and satisfies of formula (0.1). If G and all its twists $\sp{E}G,$ for G-torsors E, satisfy the above conjecture, then ${\bf H}\sbsp{d}{1}(X, G)$ satisfies the trace formula:$${\rm tr}\Phi\sb{q}\mid H\sp*({\bf H}\sbsp{d}{1},(\bar X, \bar G)\sb{\rm sm}, \doubc)={\sum\limits\sb{E\in H\sp1 (X,G)}}\ {1\over \#\rm Aut \ E}.$$In general, both sides of this equation are infinite series. This formula holds in the case that G = $GL\sb{n}$ (so that ${\bf H}\sbsp{d}{1}(X, G)$ is the stack of vector bundles of rank n and degree d), that Dyn G is connected, or that the genus of X is zero or one and G is rationally trivial.}
